i want to talk a little bit about this  what is a woman question  because it continues to be such a major  issue for the american right wing and  over the weekend at cpac which we will  cover later on in the show  the things that got the most applause  were the most overtly  homophobic and transphobic things they  were ridiculing pronouns they were  ridiculing so-called men and women  sports and on and on and on  and i want to talk about it because it's  like the big thing that republicans now  point to as their sort of gotcha what is  a woman you won't even define it and i  got a great email from a doctor of  sociolinguistics whose name is daniel i  don't want to say more i want to protect  his identity i won't even say what  country he teaches in but daniel sent me  a ton of the information and the  research that i'm incorporating into the  story so the situation is as follows the  right loves to say you liberals can't or  won't answer the simplest question what  is a woman so you can't be trusted with  anything you're not honest you're  pathetic it's such a simple question  what is a woman just answer it and if  you won't or if you can't then it shows  how bad faith and dishonest and radical  you all on the left are so let's start  with is it actually a simple question is  the question what is a woman simple to  answer the reality is that it's not and  now separately there are people saying  is the question even being asked in good  faith by the right and of course it's  not they're asking it to make a  political point they're asking it to  justify their pre-existing political  beliefs but let's put that aside is it a  simple question  defining common nouns is not actually a  simple thing  humans are terrible at defining common  nouns i'll give you an example define  apple without looking it up  all right well i mean without looking it  up i guess i'd say you know it's a round  fruit whose flesh we eat and sometimes  there's red yellow or green or orangish  sort of skin  and often it's crunchy but sometimes  it's more mealy and many of them are  sweet but some of them are tart does  that really help us identify an apple  not really there's all sorts of  exceptions there's many other fruits  which fit that definition  so then i can say well an apple is  malice domestica that's the latin name  so when i say apple what i mean is  mollusc domestica that's just circular  that's not a usable definition i'm not  really telling you anything you can use  to determine whether something you see  is or isn't an apple  now in addition  no definition that i give you  actually encompasses all the contexts  where the word apple is used the big  apple meaning new york city taking a  bite out of the apple as a sales and  marketing term getting some market share  so the reality is that it's not unique  that with the term woman we define it  differently in different contexts the  purpose of the definition is important  what are we trying to do and i'm going  to get to that in a second and in fact  as humans and people who speak english  we can often agree on what is an apple  without a definition  with the looking at the context so the  definition itself is actually not that  important so then as daniel wrote to me  the same applies when we're trying to  define a woman what are we trying to do  by defining woman or thinking about what  a woman is and it depends on the purpose  and the context consider this  if the purpose of defining woman is that  you are a man  looking to reproduce  and you're looking for a woman with whom  you can reproduce well in that  particular  case with that purpose  a trans woman with no uterus is not a  good candidate for your purposes of  defining a woman right in that context  you're talking about an individual  with the female reproductive organs so  that you can make a baby  on the other hand if you're a man  attracted to feminine individuals by  western standards then for you it might  be quite plausible that any woman  meaning a trans woman or not who has the  female form that you're attracted to is  completely and perfectly suited to the  definition of woman that's a different  purpose it's a different context and  this is where we end up with the bad  faith republican questions about what is  a woman they want common nouns defined  so that they can either discriminate  legally or so that it serves whatever  political purpose they want  now there's a big difference between an  apple and a woman with apples apples  can't make claims about whether they are  apples there's no sociocultural element  to apples when it comes to a noun like  woman we actually do have to pay  attention to  who claims to be a woman who is referred  to as a woman who is seen as a woman by  society in order to build up a working  understanding of what it is to be a  woman in society and culture this is all  completely normal republicans don't care  about it they don't care about  linguistics they care only about scoring  political points and putting other  people down so when they say it's so  simple you idiot left this just what is  a woman just give us the definition well  what is the purpose of the definition  what is the context in which you were  seeking it what are you trying to then  determine  with the definition this is normal stuff  in sociolinguistics and in many other  fields  they want to pretend  like it's not and it's as simple as just  what is an apple which by the way is not  actually so simple let me know your  thoughts you can find me on twitter at  deepakman
 

